  "question": "Pythonic News Platform\n\n 1) Background / Context\nPythonic News is an online community platform inspired by Hacker News, and it serves as a hub for Python enthusiasts. It is designed to allow members of the Python programming community to share and discuss news, articles, and projects related to Python. The platform is built using Python and Django and powers the website https://news.python.sc.\n\n 2) Objectives\n- To create a collaborative community for sharing Python-related content.\n- To facilitate discussions and engagement through a commenting system.\n- To highlight valuable content through a voting mechanism.\n- To organize content into categories, improving user navigation and content discovery.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n- Community Members: Python enthusiasts and developers who contribute and engage with the content.\n- Administrators: Oversee platform operations and manage user activities.\n- Developers: Maintain and improve the platform's functionality and user experience.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n- User Submissions: Members can submit links to Python-related content, encouraging collaboration and knowledge sharing.\n- Commenting System: Users can discuss, ask questions, and provide insights on submitted posts, fostering community engagement.\n- Voting Mechanism: Posts and comments can be upvoted or downvoted, promoting the most valuable content.\n- Content Categorization: Organizes content into categories for easier navigation and discovery.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Performance: The platform should efficiently handle a large number of users and content without performance degradation.\n- Usability: The user interface should be intuitive, enabling users to easily browse, submit, and engage with content.\n- Security: Implement secure authentication and authorization mechanisms to protect user data and platform integrity.\n- Scalability: The infrastructure should support growth in user base and functionality without significant changes to the existing system.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0038\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(150) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password_hash` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `is_admin` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `username` (`username`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `email` (`email`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `categories` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `slug` varchar(120) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(500) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `slug` (`slug`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `posts` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `category_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `url` varchar(2048) NOT NULL,\n  `summary` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `score` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `user_id` (`user_id`),\n  KEY `category_id` (`category_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `posts_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `posts_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`category_id`) REFERENCES `categories` (`id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `comments` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `parent_comment_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `body` text NOT NULL,\n  `score` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `post_id` (`post_id`),\n  KEY `user_id` (`user_id`),\n  KEY `parent_comment_id` (`parent_comment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `comments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `comments_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `comments_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`parent_comment_id`) REFERENCES `comments` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `post_votes` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `vote_value` tinyint(4) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `uniq_post_user` (`post_id`,`user_id`),\n  KEY `user_id` (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `post_votes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `posts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `post_votes_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\nCREATE TABLE `comment_votes` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `comment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `vote_value` tinyint(4) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `uniq_comment_user` (`comment_id`,`user_id`),\n  KEY `user_id` (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `comment_votes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`comment_id`) REFERENCES `comments` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `comment_votes_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
